ase, and efforts to deal with them were unsuccessful. The government then came up with the idea of giving the violence an outlet instead. \"Consensual murder\" was legalized in the year 2291, enabling people to fight to the death under organized conditions. Mining conglomerates worked with the government and organized leagues, which proved successful. One such company, the Liandri Mining Corporation, capitalized on the fights by tri-casting them; this proved to be more popular than the combat itself, their popularity increasing with brutality. By 2341, what is now called the \"Tournament\" became a professional sport more profitable than mining. Liandri Mining Corporation annually hosts the \"Grand Tournament\", the most popular event in the sport.", "summary": "Unreal Tournament is a first-person arena shooter video game developed by Epic Games and Digital Extremes. It was the second installment in the Unreal series.\n\nIt is an arena first-person shooter, with head-to-head multiplayer deathmatches being the primary focus of the game. Other game modes include TDM. CTF, Assault, Domination, Last man Standing etc.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/unreal-tournament", "videos": [{"id": 28188, "name": "Gameplay video", "video_id": "zSvTvZpeD4k", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zSvTvZpeD4k", "title": "Unreal Tournament 1999 PC", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/zSvTvZpeD4k/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 104365, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "EP-NfrP_GaM", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EP-NfrP_GaM", "title": "Unreal Tournament (ut99) Intro 1080p", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EP-NfrP_GaM/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 10121, "name": "Unreal Tournament"}]}